<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 351.6 trln lira of 357-d bills.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 351.6 trln lira of 357-d bills.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury met majority of the bids in an auction on Tuesday by selling 351.6 trillion lira nominal-valued 357-day bills at sharply higher yield.</p>
<p>It had last sold 280 trillion lira of 11-month bills at 120.37 percent yield (including witholding tax) on July 15.</p>
<p>    Amount	: 351.6 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Total bids  : 439.7 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Max yield   : 137.22 percent (including witholding tax)</p>
<p>    Maturity    : July 29, 1998</p>
<p>Value date  : August 6, 1997</p>
<p>Banks will pay 147.2 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday when the Treasury faces a 64 trillion lira t-bill redemption.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
